# HabitSense — Master's Thesis Project

## Purpose
HabitSense is a native Android research platform for the thesis:
"A RESEARCH ON THE EFFECTIVENESS OF ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE METHODS IN MONITORING AND ANALYZING USER BEHAVIOR ON ANDROID MOBILE DEVICES".

The app is **app-first, AI-enhanced**: it must work as a standard offline habit/mood/expense tracker, with analytics engines layered on top.

## Core Principles
- Kotlin + MVVM/Clean Architecture
- Offline-first local storage with Room
- Coroutines/Flow for async work
- `dateString` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) is the primary grouping key across all tables
- Strategy Pattern for analytics: baseline vs complex methods are swappable behind interfaces

## Data Layer (Completed Foundation)
Room entities:
- `HabitEntity`
- `HabitLogEntity` (unique `habitId + dateString`, binary completion)
- `MoodLogEntity` (unique `dateString`, mood 1..5)
- `ExpenseLogEntity` (multiple entries per day allowed)
- `ExperimentRunEntity` (strategy execution metrics for thesis evaluation)

Key files:
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/data/local/entity/*`
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/data/local/dao/*`
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/data/local/HabitSenseDatabase.kt`

## Feature Pipeline (Completed Foundation)
- `DailyData` aggregates one day across habits/mood/expenses
- `DailyData.activeHabitIds` distinguishes habits that existed on a date from habits that were missed
- `DailyData.completionFor(habitId)` returns `null` when a habit was not active yet
- Method-specific feature builders are preferred over one universal all-habits vector
- `HabitPredictionFeatureBuilder` produces fixed-size per-habit TFLite inputs independent of total habit count
- `ClusteringFeatureBuilder` produces fixed-size daily summary vectors for K-Means
- `FeatureSchema.VERSION` validates legacy compatibility; prediction/clustering schemas define method-specific contracts

Key files:
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/domain/model/DailyData.kt`
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/domain/model/FeatureSchema.kt`
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/data/repository/DailyDataRepository.kt`
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/domain/ai/feature/*`

## Synthetic Data (Completed Foundation)
- Seeded generator populates 6–12 months of mock data with simple distributions
- Respects DB constraints (valid habit IDs, max one mood/day)

Key files:
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/data/synthetic/SyntheticDataConfig.kt`
- `app/src/main/java/com/azizov/habitsense/data/synthetic/SyntheticDataGenerator.kt`

## AI Strategy Layer (Completed Foundation)
Interfaces:
- `HabitPredictor` (per-habit tomorrow prediction)
- `DayClusterer`
- `CorrelationAnalyzer`

Baseline implementations:
- Moving average habit predictor
- Heuristic day clusterer
- Spearman correlation analyzer

Complex implementations:
- TFLite habit predictor (`app/src/main/assets/habit_predictor.tflite`, loaded via `FileUtil.loadMappedFile`) uses fixed-size per-habit inputs
- Native Kotlin K-Means day clusterer uses fixed-size daily summary vectors
- Apriori-style association rule analyzer skips inactive habits instead of marking them missed

Switching:
- `StrategyFactory` + `StrategyMode.BASELINE|COMPLEX`

Performance tracking:
- `PerformanceProbe` captures execution time/memory
- `StrategyExecutor` persists runs in `ExperimentRunEntity`

## Planned UI Direction (Not Yet Implemented)
- Today tab: fast daily input
- Domains tab: historical charts/trends
- Insights tab: thesis intelligence screen (predictions, clusters, correlations, advice)

## Implementation Rules for Future Work
- Do not break `dateString` grouping semantics
- Do not treat a habit as missed before its `createdAtDateString`
- Keep analytics decoupled from ViewModels (domain inputs/outputs only)
- Preserve feature schema versioning when changing ML inputs or builder semantics
- Prefer method-specific feature builders for analytics inputs
- Log strategy runtime/memory for thesis evaluation on complex paths
- Prefer minimal, scoped changes; avoid unrelated refactors
